@startuml
title Implemented S3-S4 - atomic scheduling and immutable replacements
actor "Application caller / test" as Caller
participant "AppointmentRepository\nInMemoryAppointmentRepository" as Repo
participant "original : Appointment" as Original
participant "AppointmentState" as State
participant "ReservationRules" as Rules
participant "AvailabilityStrategy" as Policy
Caller -> Repo : reserve(candidate, strategy) / reschedule(id, start, strategy)
critical instance-owned ReentrantLock
  Repo -> Repo : reject nested writes; read latest values
  Repo -> Repo : capture Clock instant into fixed DomainTime
  alt reserve
    Repo -> Repo : reject duplicate ID / non-Pending / catalog mismatch
  else reschedule
    Repo -> Original : reschedule(newStart, time)
    Original -> State : requireRescheduling(originalSlot, now)
    State --> Original : eligible or exception
    Original -> Original : validate proposed slot; copy spec, retain State/subtype
    Original --> Repo : detached replacement
    Repo -> Repo : exclude only original ID from immutable schedule
  end
  Repo -> Rules : validate(candidate, strategy, schedule, time)
  Rules -> Rules : intrinsic spec validation; raw interval conflict check
  Rules -> Policy : preparationBuffer(provider)
  Policy --> Rules : zero / configured Duration
  Rules -> Rules : validate buffer and effective working hours/conflicts
  alt any failure
    Rules --> Repo : exception
    Repo --> Caller : failure; original map unchanged
  else accepted
    Rules --> Repo : immutable Reservation(appointment, buffer)
    Repo -> Repo : commit reservation + revision + append event
    Repo --> Caller : immutable appointment
  end
end
note over Repo
finally unlocks on success or failure.
find/history/reservations use the same lock and immutable values.
transition delegates finite command to latest Appointment/State,
then replaces reservation preserving buffer under the same lock.
S4 records events/revisions under this lock.
Dispatcher delivers outside it; see booking sequence.
end note
@enduml
